node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md:646:- Rendering a configurable dashboard where widgets are positioned, resized, and rearranged on a grid (built on `react-grid-layout`).
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md:647:- User-editable layouts: adding/removing widgets from an action panel, drag-and-drop, edit mode with overlay controls.
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md-648-- Plugin-based widgets where each widget type (title, text, chart, custom) is registered once and driven by a `config`.
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md-649-
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md-650-### When not to use
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md-651-
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md-652-- For a single, fixed chart or panel, use [`@gravity-ui/charts`](https://gravity-ui.com/charts) or [`@gravity-ui/chartkit`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/chartkit) directly — the grid/plugin machinery is overhead for one widget.
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md:653:- For a general-purpose responsive grid that is not a widget dashboard, use `react-grid-layout` directly.
node_modules/@gravity-ui/dashkit/README.md-654-- For embedding ChartKit-backed chart widgets inside a DashKit dashboard, DashKit is the shell; it still relies on [`@gravity-ui/chartkit`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/chartkit) to render the actual charts.
